WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.102
Build an evaluation set from real workflows using approved representative data.

00:00:05.102 --> 00:00:09.194
Include common tasks, difficult cases, ambiguous requests, stale sources,

00:00:09.194 --> 00:00:11.468
permission boundaries, and costly errors.

00:00:11.468 --> 00:00:14.196
Define expected outcomes before reviewing results.

00:00:14.196 --> 00:00:18.743
Measure answer quality, citation support, hallucinations, refusal behavior, structured output,

00:00:18.743 --> 00:00:23.745
latency, prompt processing, generation speed, memory, temperature, failure rate, and recovery.

00:00:23.745 --> 00:00:27.383
Repeat important tests because model output can vary.

00:00:27.383 --> 00:00:29.202
Test the complete application.

00:00:29.202 --> 00:00:33.749
Retrieval, document parsing, prompts, tools, API limits, authentication, interface state,

00:00:33.749 --> 00:00:38.751
and logs can fail even when the base model performs well.

00:00:38.751 --> 00:00:41.025
Track where the failure occurred.

00:00:41.025 --> 00:00:45.572
Collect user feedback tied to tasks rather than general enthusiasm.

00:00:45.572 --> 00:00:50.574
Did the assistant save time, improve quality, or create review work?

00:00:50.574 --> 00:00:56.030
Preserve examples of false confidence, missing sources, poor formatting, and unsafe actions.

00:00:56.030 --> 00:01:00.577
Model, runtime, driver, document, prompt, and configuration updates need versioning,

00:01:00.577 --> 00:01:03.760
regression tests, change approval, backups, and rollback.

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:09.672
Rebuilding an index can change answers even when the model stays the same.

00:01:09.672 --> 00:01:14.674
Monitor availability, queues, resource use, unauthorized access, data growth, stale content,

00:01:14.674 --> 00:01:16.492
errors, and quality trends.

00:01:16.492 --> 00:01:17.857
Expand users, sources,

00:01:17.857 --> 00:01:23.768
or automation only when existing workflows are reliable and operational ownership is clear.

00:01:23.768 --> 00:01:28.770
Define service objectives for uptime, latency, quality, support response, backup recovery,

00:01:28.770 --> 00:01:30.134
and index freshness.

00:01:30.134 --> 00:01:35.591
Objectives make tradeoffs visible and show when the assistant needs capacity, redesign,

00:01:35.591 --> 00:01:36.500
or retirement.
